+
+# Logic Bug Lens
+
+You are reviewing for behavioural / state-machine defects — the class of bug
+that has no single grep signature and only surfaces when you reason about
+ordering, concurrency, and edge-case inputs.
+
+HARD GATE — for every finding you MUST cite the exact trust boundary that is
+crossed: the file:line where untrusted/external input enters, and the file:line
+where the security decision is made on that input. If both sides are internal
+(service-to-service, same trust domain, idempotent retry, intentional design),
+DROP the finding. No trust-boundary citation → no finding.
+
+Reason about behaviour, don't pattern-match. Seed questions:
+- Check-then-act windows: between the permission/ownership/balance check and
+  the mutation, can a second request, another thread, or a filesystem actor
+  change what was checked?
+- Auth/session state: what does the login or step-up flow do on empty, null,
+  duplicated, or out-of-order messages? Can two concurrent requests against
+  one session leave it half-authenticated?
+- Numeric identity and counters: what happens at overflow, at zero, at
+  negative after a narrowing cast? Does an ID truncated to 32-bit collide
+  with a privileged record?
+- Connection/protocol state: can a malformed or truncated message leave the
+  parser mid-state so the NEXT request on the same connection is
+  misinterpreted?
+- Caches and memoised decisions: is the cache key missing the
+  tenant/user/role dimension, so one principal's result is served to
+  another? Does a cached "authorised" decision outlive a revocation?
+- Sentinel return values: is the result of indexOf/find/search (which returns
+  -1 / null when the token is absent) used as an offset or length WITHOUT the
+  `== -1` guard, so "not found" silently becomes position 0 or a wrong
+  substring slice? Same for parseInt→NaN or a lookup returning null treated as
+  success.
diff -ruN a/.vvaharness/skills/missing-controls/SKILL.md b/.vvaharness/skills/missing-controls/SKILL.md
--- a/.vvaharness/skills/missing-controls/SKILL.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/.vvaharness/skills/missing-controls/SKILL.md	2026-10-27 12:15:24.024859275 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@
+---
+name: missing-controls
+description: Find weaknesses that consist of an ABSENT control — no rate limit, no session invalidation, no cookie flags, debug left on, secrets or PII stored in cleartext — by enumerating every site the control belongs and checking each.
+---
+
+<!--
+Copyright 2026 Visa, Inc.
+
+Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
+you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.
+You may obtain a copy of the License at
+
+	http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
+
+Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
+distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS,
+WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.
+See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
+limitations under the License.
+-->
+
+# Absent-Control Lens
+
+Every other lens hunts for a dangerous **construct** — a sink, a concatenation, a weak
+algorithm. This lens hunts for a **hole**. You cannot grep for a decorator that was never
+written, and a deterministic scanner will never hand you a line number for it, so nothing
+upstream will point you at these. If you only investigate what you were shown, you will
+never report one.
+
+The method is inverted. Instead of "is this construct dangerous?", ask **"what should be
+here, and is it?"** That requires enumerating sites first and judging second.
+
+## Hard gate — a finding requires all three
+
+1. **The site is real and reachable.** A concrete handler, route, cookie write, session
+   config, or storage write that an external actor can reach. Not a hypothetical.
+2. **The control genuinely belongs there.** Name the asset it would protect and the actor
+   it would stop. "Every endpoint should have rate limiting" is not analysis; "`/api/login`
+   accepts unlimited password guesses against a user-supplied username" is.
+3. **It is absent on THIS path**, and you checked — not merely "not visible in the file you
+   were given". Middleware, a base class, a decorator factory, a reverse-proxy config, or a
+   framework default can supply it somewhere you have not looked yet. Look, then conclude.
+
+If the control exists anywhere on the path, **refute** and say where it is. A refutation
+here is a real result: it is how the FP rate stays low.
+
+## Enumerate before you conclude
+
+These are systemic gaps, and a systemic gap is only actionable if the site list is
+complete. Reporting one unprotected route while four others are equally exposed means
+whoever applies your fix still ships the vulnerability.
+
+So for each control below: **Grep the whole repository for every site of the kind it
+protects, then decide site by site.** Report one finding per absent site, each with its own
+file and line. If it is present everywhere you enumerated, refute and say how many sites
+you checked.
+
+## The controls, and where each belongs
+
+### Anti-automation on credential and cost endpoints — CWE-307, CWE-799
+**Sites:** every handler that verifies a credential or consumes a scarce resource — login,
+registration, password reset, OTP/MFA verification, token refresh, email send, payment,
+file upload, expensive search.
+**Present looks like:** `flask-limiter` `@limiter.limit(...)`; `django-ratelimit`
+`@ratelimit`; DRF throttle classes; `slowapi` on FastAPI; `express-rate-limit`; Spring
+`Bucket4j`; a failed-attempt counter with lockout persisted per account **or** per source;
+a CAPTCHA gate; an upstream WAF/gateway rule **only if you can see it in this repo**.
+**Note:** a `LoginAttempt` model or a `failed_count` column existing is not the control —
+find the code that *reads* it and *refuses*. Storage without enforcement is a decoy.
+
+### Session termination — CWE-613, CWE-384
+**Sites:** logout, password change, email change, role change, account deactivation.
+**Present looks like:** server-side session destroy (`session.clear()`,
+`request.session.flush()`, store delete); for stateless JWT a denylist/`jti` revocation
+check, or a `token_version`/`password_changed_at` claim compared on every request.
+**The classic hole:** a logout endpoint that returns `200 {"message": "logged out"}` and
+nothing else, while the issued JWT stays valid until expiry — the token is still a working
+credential. Also: a password change that does not invalidate other live sessions, and a
+session with no absolute or idle lifetime at all.
+
+### Cookie and transport flags — CWE-614, CWE-1004, CWE-1275, CWE-319
+**Sites:** every `set_cookie` / `Set-Cookie` write **and** every framework session config
+key. There are usually more of these than you expect; grep for all of them.
+**Present looks like:** `httponly=True`, `secure=True`, `samesite="Lax"` or `"Strict"` on
+each write; `SESSION_COOKIE_HTTPONLY` / `_SECURE` / `_SAMESITE`; Django
+`SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT`, `SECURE_HSTS_SECONDS`.
+**Report per site.** A config-level default does not cover an explicit `set_cookie` that
+overrides it, and fixing the config does not fix the explicit writes.
+
+### Deployment and debug posture — CWE-16, CWE-215, CWE-489
+**Sites:** app entrypoints, settings modules, Dockerfiles, compose files, CI/CD manifests.
+**The holes:** `app.run(debug=True)` — the Werkzeug console is remote code execution, and
+`host="0.0.0.0"` makes it reachable; Django `DEBUG = True`; `ALLOWED_HOSTS = ["*"]`;
+stack traces or exception detail returned to the client; verbose error handlers;
+directory listing; admin or metrics endpoints exposed without auth; default credentials
+left in a seed or fixture.
+**On CWE choice:** report the class your evidence supports. If debug mode yields arbitrary
+code execution, that is what it yields — say so, and name the misconfiguration as the
+cause in your description so both readings are recoverable.
+
+### Data at rest and in transit — CWE-312, CWE-311, CWE-319, CWE-359
+**Sites:** model/schema definitions, migrations, seed and fixture data, serializers,
+cache and queue writes, log statements, backup and export paths.
+**The holes:** identifiers and PII (national ID, DOB, full address, card data, health
+data) stored as plain columns or plain JSON blobs; a seed/fixture that commits real-looking
+sensitive values; secrets written to a cache or queue unencrypted; TLS verification
+disabled on an outbound call (`verify=False`, `rejectUnauthorized: false`).
+**Distinguish:** stored-in-cleartext (CWE-312) is a different finding from
+returned-in-a-response (CWE-359/200) even for the same field. If both hold, both are
+findings — they have different fixes and different blast radii.
+
+### Request forgery and origin trust — CWE-352, CWE-942, CWE-1021
+Covered in depth by the `csrf` lens; treat it as part of this sweep when the claim is that
+a *protection is missing* rather than that a sink is dangerous. **Enumerate every
+state-changing handler**, not just the one you were pointed at.
+
+### Authorization
+Covered by the `access-control` lens, which already frames it as an absence. Note its
+"where to look" examples are Spring/JAX-RS; translate to the framework in front of you —
+Flask `@login_required` / `before_request`, Django permission classes and mixins, FastAPI
+`Depends(...)`, Express middleware.
+
+## False-positive discipline
+
+Refute, do not report, when:
+
+- The control is present anywhere on the path, including in middleware, a base class, a
+  dependency, a decorator applied at the blueprint/router level, or a framework default
+  you can point to.
+- The endpoint is genuinely public and unauthenticated by design (health check, static
+  asset, public docs, webhook with signature verification present) and holds no scarce
+  resource.
+- The "sensitive" data is obviously synthetic test fixture data **and** the file is not
+  shipped or seeded into a running environment. If it *is* seeded, it is a finding.
+- The target is a fixed constant rather than attacker-varied — bounded blast radius, do
+  not inflate it.
+
+Say which of these you checked. An absence claim with no stated search is indistinguishable
+from a guess, and the reader cannot tell them apart.
+
+## What good output looks like
+
+One finding per absent site, each naming the file and the line the fix must edit — the
+handler signature or decorator line for a missing guard, the `set_cookie` call for a
+missing flag, the settings line for a posture problem. The rationale states what you
+enumerated, how many sites you found, which had the control and which did not.
diff -ruN a/.vvaharness/skills/missing-controls/probe.sh b/.vvaharness/skills/missing-controls/probe.sh
--- a/.vvaharness/skills/missing-controls/probe.sh	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/.vvaharness/skills/missing-controls/probe.sh	2026-10-27 12:15:24.025123767 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,163 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Absent-control probe: enumerates every site a control belongs (routes, cookie writes, storage,
+# config) and every place the control is actually present, so absence can be proven per site.
+
+# Copyright 2026 Visa, Inc.
+#
+# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
+# you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.
+# You may obtain a copy of the License at
+#
+#     http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
+#
+# Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
+# distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS,
+# WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.
+# See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
+# limitations under the License.
+
+set -f
+ROOT=${1:-.}
+CAP=${MC_PROBE_CAP:-12}
+WIDTH=140
+EX="--exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=.venv --exclude-dir=venv
+--exclude-dir=.tox --exclude-dir=dist --exclude-dir=build --exclude-dir=__pycache__
+--exclude-dir=site-packages --exclude-dir=.mypy_cache --exclude-dir=target
+--exclude-dir=.next --exclude-dir=coverage
+--exclude-dir=.vvaharness --exclude-dir=security-scan --exclude=SKILL.md --exclude=probe.sh"
+
+# scan LABEL "INCLUDE_GLOBS" "ERE" — capped path:line hits, or (none).
+scan() {
+	_label=$1
+	_globs=$2
+	_pat=$3
+	_inc=
+	for _g in $_globs; do _inc="$_inc --include=$_g"; done
+	echo "== $_label =="
+	_out=$(grep -rEn --binary-files=without-match $_inc $EX -- "$_pat" "$ROOT" 2>/dev/null || true)
+	if [ -z "$_out" ]; then
+		echo "(none)"
+	else
+		_n=$(printf '%s\n' "$_out" | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
+		printf '%s\n' "$_out" | head -n "$CAP" | cut -c1-$WIDTH
+		[ "$_n" -gt "$CAP" ] && echo "... $_n hits total, showing $CAP - grep this pattern yourself for the rest"
+	fi
+	echo ""
+}
+
+# scan2 LABEL "INCLUDE_GLOBS" "ERE" "ERE2" — hits matching both patterns (site AND keyword).
+scan2() {
+	_label=$1
+	_globs=$2
+	_pat=$3
+	_pat2=$4
+	_inc=
+	for _g in $_globs; do _inc="$_inc --include=$_g"; done
+	echo "== $_label =="
+	_out=$(grep -rEn --binary-files=without-match $_inc $EX -- "$_pat" "$ROOT" 2>/dev/null |
+		grep -iE -- "$_pat2" || true)
+	if [ -z "$_out" ]; then
+		echo "(none)"
+	else
+		_n=$(printf '%s\n' "$_out" | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
+		printf '%s\n' "$_out" | head -n "$CAP" | cut -c1-$WIDTH
+		[ "$_n" -gt "$CAP" ] && echo "... $_n hits total, showing $CAP - grep this pattern yourself for the rest"
+	fi
+	echo ""
+}
+
+# files LABEL "INCLUDE_GLOBS" "ERE" — file names only (existence is the answer, not the lines).
+files() {
+	_label=$1
+	_globs=$2
+	_pat=$3
+	_inc=
+	for _g in $_globs; do _inc="$_inc --include=$_g"; done
+	echo "== $_label =="
+	_out=$(grep -rlE --binary-files=without-match $_inc $EX -- "$_pat" "$ROOT" 2>/dev/null || true)
+	if [ -z "$_out" ]; then
+		echo "(none)"
+	else
+		_n=$(printf '%s\n' "$_out" | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
+		printf '%s\n' "$_out" | head -n 15
+		[ "$_n" -gt 15 ] && echo "... $_n files total, showing 15"
+	fi
+	echo ""
+}
+
+ROUTE='@[a-zA-Z_.]*\.(route|get|post|put|patch|delete)\(|@(Get|Post|Put|Patch|Delete|Request)Mapping|(app|router|api|server)\.(get|post|put|patch|delete|all)\(|path\(|re_path\(|url\(|def (get|post|put|patch|delete)\(|\[Http(Get|Post|Put|Delete)\]'
+SENSITIVE='ssn|social_security|national_id|tax_id|passport|dob|date_of_birth|birth|card_number|cardnum|pan\b|cvv|cvc|iban|routing|account_number|salary|income|health|diagnosis|medical|insurance|address|phone|mobile|email|api_key|apikey|secret|token|password|passwd|pin\b|license'
+
+echo "### MISSING-CONTROLS PROBE root=$ROOT"
+echo ""
+
+CAP=15
+echo "--- SITES: enumerate these, then judge each ---"
+echo ""
+
+scan "ALL ROUTE/HANDLER SITES (total count is your enumeration denominator)" "" "$ROUTE"
+
+scan2 "CREDENTIAL AND COST ENDPOINTS (rate-limit sites)" "" "$ROUTE" \
+	'login|signin|sign_in|logout|signout|register|signup|sign_up|password|reset|forgot|otp|mfa|2fa|verify|token|refresh|confirm|invite|upload|import|export|search|send|mail|sms|pay|charge|checkout|transfer|withdraw'
+
+scan2 "STATE-CHANGING HANDLERS (CSRF / authz enumeration sites)" "" "$ROUTE" \
+	'post|put|patch|delete|create|update|edit|save|add|remove|transfer|change|reset'
+
+scan "COOKIE WRITE SITES (one finding per write; config default does not cover these)" "" \
+	'set_cookie|Set-Cookie|res\.cookie|response\.cookies|addCookie|new Cookie\(|HttpCookie|cookies\.set|\.cookie\s*='
+
+scan "SESSION AND TOKEN CONFIG SITES" "" \
+	'SESSION_COOKIE_[A-Z]+|CSRF_COOKIE_[A-Z]+|REMEMBER_COOKIE_[A-Z]+|PERMANENT_SESSION_LIFETIME|SESSION_COOKIE_AGE|SESSION_EXPIRE|session\.permanent|JWT_|jwt\.(encode|sign)|expires_delta|exp[\"'\'']?\s*[:=]|maxAge|max_age|SECRET_KEY|secret\s*[:=]'
+
+scan2 "STORAGE SITES HOLDING SENSITIVE FIELDS (cleartext-at-rest sites)" "" \
+	'Column\(|db\.Column|models\.[A-Za-z]+Field\(|@Column|Schema\(|Field\(|CREATE TABLE|ALTER TABLE|ADD COLUMN|add_column|INSERT INTO' \
+	"$SENSITIVE"
+
+files "SEED / FIXTURE / SAMPLE DATA FILES (synthetic only refutes if never seeded)" \
+	"*seed* *fixture* *sample* *demo* *.sql *.csv" \
+	'INSERT INTO|password|api_key|secret|ssn|card|token'
+
+files "CONFIG AND DEPLOYMENT FILES PRESENT (open these for posture)" \
+	"Dockerfile* docker-compose* *.yml *.yaml *.ini *.cfg *.toml *.env* Procfile *.tf settings*.py config*.py" \
+	'DEBUG|debug|host|HOST|port|PORT|ENV|environment|image:|command:'
+
+CAP=6
+echo "--- CONTROLS: where each is actually present ---"
+echo ""
+
+scan "RATE LIMIT / ANTI-AUTOMATION PRESENT" "" \
+	'limiter|Limiter|@ratelimit|ratelimit|RateLimit|rate_limit|throttle|Throttle|slowapi|express-rate-limit|Bucket4j|resilience4j|captcha|recaptcha|hcaptcha|turnstile|failed_(attempt|count|login)s?|login_attempt|LoginAttempt|lockout|locked_until|backoff'
+
+scan "AUTH / AUTHZ GUARDS PRESENT" "" \
+	'login_required|@login|jwt_required|token_required|auth_required|requires_auth|requireAuth|isAuthenticated|IsAuthenticated|permission_classes|has_permission|@PreAuthorize|@Secured|@RolesAllowed|before_request|Depends\(|middleware\.[Aa]uth|passport\.|ensureLoggedIn|current_user|\[Authorize\]'
+
+scan "SESSION TERMINATION / REVOCATION PRESENT" "" \
+	'session\.(clear|flush|pop|destroy|invalidate)|logout_user|destroy_session|invalidateSession|revoke|revocation|jti|token_version|password_changed_at|denylist|blocklist|blacklist|deleted_tokens|refresh_token_rotation'
+
+scan "COOKIE FLAGS AND TRANSPORT SECURITY PRESENT" "" \
+	'httponly|HttpOnly|[Ss]ecure\s*[:=]|samesite|SameSite|SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT|SECURE_HSTS|Strict-Transport-Security|HSTS|force_https|SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE|PREFERRED_URL_SCHEME'
+
+scan "CSRF PROTECTION PRESENT" "" \
+	'CSRFProtect|CsrfViewMiddleware|csrf_token|csrf_exempt|WTF_CSRF|csurf|csrf-token|X-CSRF|XSRF|AntiForgery|@csrf'
+
+scan "SECURITY HEADERS PRESENT" "" \
+	'Content-Security-Policy|X-Frame-Options|X-Content-Type-Options|Referrer-Policy|Permissions-Policy|Talisman|helmet|frame_options|X-XSS-Protection'
+
+scan "PASSWORD / FIELD ENCRYPTION PRIMITIVES PRESENT" "" \
+	'bcrypt|argon2|pbkdf2|scrypt|generate_password_hash|check_password_hash|werkzeug\.security|passlib|PasswordEncoder|Fernet|AES|KMS|encrypt|EncryptedType|pgcrypto'
+
+CAP=12
+echo "--- POSTURE HOLES: these hits are usually findings on sight ---"
+echo ""
+
+scan "DEBUG / EXPOSURE POSTURE" "" \
+	'debug\s*=\s*True|DEBUG\s*=\s*True|debug:\s*true|app\.run\(|ALLOWED_HOSTS\s*=|\*.{0,3}ALLOWED|host\s*=\s*.0\.0\.0\.0|--reload|FLASK_ENV|FLASK_DEBUG|NODE_ENV|display_errors|expose_php|printStackTrace|print_exc|traceback\.format_exc|autoreload|werkzeug'
+
